      "caption": {
        "body": "Marshall Moxom (1916–2007) was a San Francisco-based photographer active between the late 1930s and mid-1970s. During his tenure with the San Francisco Public Utilities Commission (PUC), Moxom frequently worked at San Francisco International Airport (SFO), where he made aerial photographs and documented terminal construction, events, and airport personnel.   Today, SFO Museum holds approximately 750 photographic negatives made by Moxom while on assignment at the Airport. See “Above SFO: The Aerial Photography of Marshall Moxom” on display, pre-security, in Harvey Milk Terminal 1 or online at:  https://bit.ly/4d5sOAh  📸: Photographer Marshall Moxom [left] and Ken Snodgrass posing in front of a Cessna 175, San Francisco International Airport (SFO), February 19, 1960; view facing north with San Bruno Mountain visible on horizon  Collection of SFO Museum;  2011.032.0609  R2022.0901.005",
